**************** CORNERS OF CAPACITORS (ihp-sg13cmos5l) ****************
* cmos5l has two capacitors, both metal-oxide-metal on the Metal1..Metal4 stack
* (the MIM caps cmim/rfcmim need the forbidden MIM layer and are excluded):
*   cap_cmomi   IHP's interdigitated MoM, with a feed topology and a full RF
*               equivalent circuit.
*   cap_cmomf   the metal fringe (finger) variant, EM-fitted.
* Both are OSDI compact models; their 2-terminal wrapper subckts live in
* cap_cmomi.lib and cap_cmomf.lib, and the OSDI objects auto-load via
* libs.tech/ngspice/.spiceinit.
*
* NOTE (caveat, see each wrapper lib and Verilog-A header): neither device has a
* corner or mismatch spread characterised on silicon.  cap_cmomi carries the
* g2-derived NOMINAL coefficients transferred by layer count (bar the single-side
* feed term, fitted in-house) and maps to the same nominal model in every section
* below.  This is not a claim of corner-stability; its spread is simply not
* modelled (pending silicon).  cap_cmomf carries an EM-fitted capacitance and
* estimated spreads, set by the cmomf_* parameters below after its include.  As in
* g2, bcs is low C and wcs is high C.  The section names mirror g2's cornerCAP.lib
* so a corner sweep written against g2 resolves unchanged.
***********************************************************************

* Typical without statistical modeling
.LIB cap_typ
.include cap_cmomi.lib
.include cap_cmomf.lib
.ENDL cap_typ

* Typical with mismatch modeling (nominal: no characterised mismatch)
.LIB cap_typ_mismatch
.include cap_cmomi.lib
.include cap_cmomf.lib
.param cmomf_mm=1
.ENDL cap_typ_mismatch

* Typical with statistical modeling (nominal: no characterised spread)
.LIB cap_typ_stat
.include cap_cmomi.lib
.include cap_cmomf.lib
.param mc_cmomf_cscale='gauss(1, 0.045, 1)'
.param cmomf_cscale=mc_cmomf_cscale
.param cmomf_rscale='pow(cmomf_cscale, -1.5)'
.ENDL cap_typ_stat

* Best Case without statistical modeling (nominal)
.LIB cap_bcs
.include cap_cmomi.lib
.include cap_cmomf.lib
.param cmomf_cscale=0.87 cmomf_rscale=1.25
.ENDL cap_bcs

* Best Case with mismatch modeling (nominal)
.LIB cap_bcs_mismatch
.include cap_cmomi.lib
.include cap_cmomf.lib
.param cmomf_cscale=0.87 cmomf_rscale=1.25 cmomf_mm=1
.ENDL cap_bcs_mismatch

* Worst Case without statistical modeling (nominal)
.LIB cap_wcs
.include cap_cmomi.lib
.include cap_cmomf.lib
.param cmomf_cscale=1.17 cmomf_rscale=0.80
.ENDL cap_wcs

* Worst Case with mismatch modeling (nominal)
.LIB cap_wcs_mismatch
.include cap_cmomi.lib
.include cap_cmomf.lib
.param cmomf_cscale=1.17 cmomf_rscale=0.80 cmomf_mm=1
.ENDL cap_wcs_mismatch
